## ⚙️ One Manual Step YOU Need to Do

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Supabase SQL** — Run this one line in your Supabase SQL Editor before I start. This lets the `visit_products` table be queried for "days of stock" calculation (it already exists, just needs to be included in a query — actually **no migration needed at all**). ✅

**No SQL migration required.** All 5 features compute from existing tables:
- `customer_visits` → churn dates, revenue insights
- `visit_services` → top services, service recommender
- `visit_products` → days of stock calculation  
